  {
   "id": "concept-sound",
   "label": "Sound File Size",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Sound File Size</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A sound file stores one sample for every sample taken, so its size depends on how many samples there are and how many bits each one needs.</p><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>File size in bits</strong> = sample rate &times; sample resolution &times; length of the track in seconds</li><li>Sample rate is samples per second, sample resolution is bits per sample.</li><li>Then use the same ladder: divide by 8 for bytes, by 1024 for KiB, by 1024 again for MiB.</li><li>A track length in minutes must be changed to seconds first.</li></ul>"
  },
