   "validatorKey": "y10_1_3_l2_exam_sound",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam-Style Question: Sound File Size</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Adapted from the image calculation in Cambridge IGCSE 0478/12, March 2026, Question 1(b), using a sound file. None of the Paper 1 questions in this set asks for a sound file size. A sound file is recorded with a sample rate of 8192 samples per second and a sample resolution of 16 bits. The track is 64 seconds long.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y10-13l2-exam-sound-a\">(a) Calculate the file size of the sound file in KiB. Show your working. [2]</label><input id=\"y10-13l2-exam-sound-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-sound-a\" aria-label=\"Exam-Style Question: Sound File Size part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y10-13l2-exam-sound-b\">(b) Give the same file size in MiB. [1]</label><input id=\"y10-13l2-exam-sound-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-sound-b\" aria-label=\"Exam-Style Question: Sound File Size part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y10-13l2-exam-sound-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y10-13l2-exam-sound-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"
